What is this?
\b0 \
	This is not a chronology, but alphabetical. If you want things in chronological order, go to to the DC chronology. It's not a competition. When the chronology 2.0 starts, it will be a great thing for DC fans. But if you just want a Bunch of Batman, Worship Wonder Woman, are Starry Eyed for Starman, want to Team up with the Titans, Just like the Justice League. Love the Legion \'85. I'll spare you any more \'85 you can do that more easily with an alphabetical version. Plus the Pre-DC and Post-DC are not in the DC chronology. (see below)\
\
	
\b This will be every scanned comic that was published/distributed by DC Including all the other names it put on covers instead of DC. 
\b0 Thats's mostly the same list as the chronology, but perhaps not exactly. A partial list of imprints is Vertigo (ugghh!)\'ae, Wildstorm, Helix, Milestone, Minx, Paradox, Piranha, Tangent, America's Best Comics, Cliffhanger, CMX, Homage, Humanoids, and MC.Gaines (Mad Magazine). Some were not actually produced by DC, just distributed. I have seen up to 46 different names listed but many of these are picky distinctions and are regular DC to most people.\
	
\b I'll include most alternate covers, but not look hard for them.
\b0  If I have 3 covers but the there are 4, I'm too lazy to even find out what name I should search for it under. Strong I am with the sharing, but not that strong. Many are in with the comics themselves, but not all are so labeled. I also am not going to worry about covers from TPB and HC reprints, though again I have most, at least in small form. \
	Amended - starting about part 3 I started getting all TPB & HC covers. I might miss some I don't know about. Starting about part 10 I slacked off again. You can get most for your self at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://dcomics.com"}}{\fldrslt dcomics.com}}. Google image search will get you any others.\
\
	
\b It will include many related comics such as comics in which characters appeared before they were published by DC,
\b0  aka "Pre-DC", and occasionally "Post-DC". There's a lot more of this sort of thing than you might think. Major Pre-DC characters include Blackhawk, Plastic Man, Blue Beetle and Captain Marvel (aka Shazam!) Many lessor DC figures and titles also started Pre-DC. Many things that aren't mainstream DC Universe (e.g. Loony Tunes. StarTrek) will have earlier appearances included. Even I don't know the full list yet.\
	Plus anything else related I think worthy of tossing in. Books about DC, Trading Cards, Parodies, all kinds of miscellaneous stuff. \
\
	
\b So it's the complete DC, and yet much more.
\b0 \
\
	
\b I am tracking down as much of the CMX imprint which is Manga as I can.
\b0  In most cases where I can't find it or it is unscanned, I have been able to find scanlations of the original Japanese editions as a substitute. Scanlation is the term for a comic translated by volunteers rather than the publishers..  It is scanned, then has as much of the original language text is removed as can be without destroying the art.  Next another language is put in place of it. Translators may not be the same as the scanner. Sometimes the translators (much thanks to them as this is a lot of unpaid work) are not sufficiently fluent in both languages to do as well as the professionals. In some cases, hopefully most, the translation is checked by a native speaker of the new language for grammar and readability. In other cases you can tell that this did not happen as word choice or word order is a bit off.  So same art and story. but translation wording and quality vary from the commercial versions. In a few cases CMX versions had some art redrawn (by the original artist) to conform to US sensibilities so they would be accepted without being  shrink-wrap in mainstream bookstores. (Female nipples are of the Devil himself, that sort of thing). If I paid attention to which those were I'd try to offer both versions. But I'm spending so much time finding the CMX or substitutions that I'm not paying attention to that. In some case I have to download hundreds of pages one by one, then put in a cbr file.\
	Some CMX scans I've found are un-cropped. The page is the size of the scanner bed, leaving huge margins. Since these are hundreds of pages, I just don't have time to fix this. If anyone of you does this and gets them to me, I will gladly post revised versions in a fill torrent.\
	BTW, scanlation is being done for comics from Europe as well as Manga. The only other thing I can think of off hand that DC published that had to be translated is the Humanoids stuff from France. Some of that is unscanned and it's less likely I can find a scanlation. There is much less demand for translations of comics from countries other than Japan.\
 \
